// Jahshaka fog — Ogre's fog block with Jahshaka's authorable colour, a
// height-varying second layer, and the planet's atmosphere's aerial perspective.
//
// WHO DOES WHAT
//   * The distance term under every sky but the atmosphere is upstream's:
//     OgreScene registers OUR atmosphere component (Atmosphere.h, an
//     Ogre::AtmosphereComponent) on the SceneManager, which sets the hlms_fog
//     property and binds its own const buffer (declared below as the piece the
//     stock shaders insert, AtmosphereNprSkyStructDecl). The stock Pbs pixel
//     shader then does
//         fogWeight = exp2( -eyeDistance * fogDensity )   (plus the brightness
//                     "breakthrough" term), colour = lerp( inPs.fog.xyz, colour, w )
//     and we never maintain that code.
//   * The COLOUR is ours: upstream's per-vertex sky colour piece is replaced by
//     the authored fog colour out of the pass buffer.
//   * HEIGHT FOG is ours, applied after the built-in fog. Two absorbing layers of the
//     same colour compose exactly by multiplying their transmittances, so a second
//     lerp toward the same colour is not an approximation of "one combined density"
//     — it IS it:  lerp(F, lerp(F, S, T1), T2) = F + (S-F)*T1*T2.
//   * UNDER THE PLANET'S ATMOSPHERE (jah_atmo_ap, SKY-ATMOSPHERE-1) the whole
//     fog is per pixel, below: the air first — the aerial-perspective table at
//     the pixel's direction and distance — then the World fog and its height
//     layer on top, towards the sky just above the horizon.
//
// THIS FILE IS AN Hlms LIBRARY FILE, not a per-datablock custom piece: the folder is
// appended to HlmsPbs's library paths in OgreEngine::ensureHlms(). That is what lets
// ONE file define pieces for BOTH shader stages (the _piece_vs_piece_ps name) — a
// per-datablock custom piece is attached per stage, and the pass-buffer members must
// be declared identically in the vertex and pixel shader or the two stages disagree
// about the layout of a buffer they both read. Verified against a real shader dump
// (JAHSHAKA_HLMS_DEBUG_DIR): PassBuffer is generated from one property set, so the
// vertex and pixel copies are byte-identical up to this insertion point.
//
// CAUTION for editors: the Hlms parser does NOT respect // comments — an at-directive
// inside a comment is still executed. Never write one here.
//
// The pass-buffer members below are appended to the END of the PassData struct and
// filled by FogHlmsListener (OgreFog.cpp); the two layouts line up by construction.
// They exist only when fog is on: fog off (under any sky but the atmosphere)
// unregisters the component, which drops hlms_fog, which removes every line of
// this file from the generated shader — the bit-exact "no fog" the offscreen
// pixel suites depend on.

// THE PASS-BUFFER EXTENSION, and it is ONE piece for two features (the parser
// fails the whole shader on a duplicate piece NAME, so there can only ever be
// one definition of this in the tree — see the emitter's allowed-piece list,
// HLMS_ADOPTION_SPEC section 7.4). NOTE, and the file says so above: an
// at-directive inside a comment is EXECUTED, so this block spells the
// directives out in words.
//
// LAYOUT IS THE WHOLE GAME HERE. One pass buffer is shared by every material in
// a pass; each shader declares its OWN view of it, and those views must agree
// on every offset up to the last field a shader reads. FogHlmsListener writes
// all 24 floats unconditionally, so the field ORDER below is fixed:
// (While an irradiance field is bound the host SKIPS four floats before writing
// any of this, because the renderer's own IrradianceField block under-reports
// its size by exactly that much and its last float4 would otherwise be
// overwritten. Nothing is declared here for those four: the shader's
// IrradianceField struct already occupies them, which is the whole discrepancy.
// The long argument is on FogHlmsListener::ifdAlignFloats, OgreFog.cpp.)
//   [0..3]  fog colour + height density   (declared only when the fog is on)
//   [4..7]  fog height terms + the analytic sky's distance density (ditto)
//   [8..11] the shader clock              (declared only for materials that
//                                          carry a generated piece)
//   [12..15] the DDGI block                (declared only while an
//                                          IrradianceField is bound)
//   [16..19] the environment's gain + mips (declared only by a pass that
//                                          claimed the environment's extra
//                                          texture slot -- jah_env)
// A material with a piece therefore has to declare PADDING for the fog fields
// when the fog is off, or its clock would read the fog colour — and the same
// rule one field further out: anything declaring jahIfd must first declare
// everything before it, which is why the clock's block is entered for the
// field's sake too (its contents are then padding, never read).
//
// `jah_shader_clock` is OUR OWN datablock property (setCustomProperties in
// OgreMaterials.cpp), set only on materials that carry a generated shader
// piece. `irradiance_field` is UPSTREAM's pass property, set by HlmsPbs only
// while a field is bound. Both gates keep every other material's generated
// source BYTE-IDENTICAL to a build where none of this existed.
@piece( custom_passBuffer )
	@property( hlms_fog )
		float4 jahFogColour;	// rgb = fog colour (linear; not read under the atmosphere), w = height-layer density (0 = off)
		float4 jahFogHeight;	// x = height falloff, y = reference world Y, z = camera world Y, w = the World fog's distance density under the atmosphere
	@end
	@property( jah_shader_clock || irradiance_field || jah_env )
		@property( !hlms_fog )
			float4 jahFogColourUnused;
			float4 jahFogHeightUnused;
		@end
		float4 jahClock;		// x = seconds since the host's clock started; yzw reserved
	@end
	@property( irradiance_field )
		float3 jahIfd;			// JahIfd_piece_ps.any: x = the field's window offset,
								// packed x + 128 y + 16384 z (PHOTON-WRITER-1's
								// scroll), yz = the field's Y and Z probe counts
								// (upstream's own block carries only Nx and Nx*Ny,
								// and the visibility threshold needs all three axes).
								// THREE floats: std140 aligns the next float4 to 16,
								// so the host writes one pad float after them
	@end
	@property( jah_env )
		@property( !irradiance_field )
			float4 jahIfdUnused;
		@end
		float4 jahEnv;			// THE ONE ENVIRONMENT (PHOTON-ENV-1): rgb = the cube's
								// gain per channel (the Sky Light's intensity times its
								// tint), w = the cube's own mip count. The gain cannot
								// ride ambientUpperHemi.w: that pass scale is a single
								// channel, and it is pinned to 1.0 while a probe grid is
								// bound because it also scales the probe samples.
	@end
	@property( jah_cloud_shadow )
		// THE CLOUD LAYER'S GROUND SHADOW (CLOUDS-2D-1), the LAST members, so
		// everything before them is padded when its own feature is absent --
		// the same declare-everything-before-you rule as the blocks above.
		@property( !jah_shader_clock && !irradiance_field && !jah_env )
			@property( !hlms_fog )
				float4 jahCloudPadFogColour;
				float4 jahCloudPadFogHeight;
			@end
			float4 jahCloudPadClock;
		@end
		@property( !irradiance_field && !jah_env )
			float4 jahCloudPadIfd;
		@end
		@property( !jah_env )
			float4 jahCloudPadEnv;
		@end
		float4 jahCloudInvView0;	// the pass camera's view-to-world transform, rows
		float4 jahCloudInvView1;	// x, y and z (the pixel shader has only the
		float4 jahCloudInvView2;	// view-space position of the fragment)
		float4 jahCloudMap;			// x = 1 / tile (1/m), y = shadow strength, zw = scroll (m)
		float4 jahCloudSun;			// xy = toSun.xz / toSun.y, z = altitude (m), w = 1 / mu_s
	@end
@end

// THE ENVIRONMENT CUBE (PHOTON-ENV-1; first claimed by fork 4d5fbef16+8f09c0cd4 (was 0048), lane
// SKY-FALLBACK-1, for the probe-array pass alone). Every escape in the pixel
// shader reads it now -- the voxel cones' (jah_environment.glsl through
// Vct_piece_ps.any) and the probe-array pass's no-probe fallback.
//
// Declared here rather than in upstream's PixelShader_ps.glsl because upstream
// offers the hook: custom_ps_uniformDeclaration sits immediately after the
// pass/material struct declarations and before every texture of upstream's own.
// The register number is whatever HlmsPbs reserved for the listener's one extra
// pass texture, published as a property by
// FogHlmsListener::propertiesMergedPreGenerationStep, and the sampler shares
// the index (CbTexture binds both at one unit).
//
// It exists only in a pass that claimed the slot: a colour pass of a scene that
// has an environment cube lit by its Sky Light AND a reader of it (a voxel
// volume bound, or a probe grid holding the env-probe slot).
// GATHER-0 (2026-09-21) shares this piece, and MUST: `custom_ps_uniformDeclaration`
// may be defined ONCE per permutation, and both the sky's extra slot and the
// screen-probe gather's can be live in the same pass. So the two declarations
// live in one definition, each under its own property, and the file that owns
// the piece is this one. The gather's register is claimed beside the sky's in
// FogHlmsListener::propertiesMergedPreGenerationStep, in the fixed order
// getNumExtraPassTextures states.
@property( jah_env || jah_probe_gather || jah_cloud_shadow || jah_sun_contact || jah_atmo_ap )
@piece( custom_ps_uniformDeclaration )
	@property( jah_env )
		vulkan_layout( ogre_t@value(jahEnvCube) ) midf_tex uniform textureCube jahEnvCube;
		@property( syntax == glslvk )
			layout( ogre_s@value(jahEnvCube) ) uniform sampler jahEnvSampler;
		@end
	@end
	// The DECLARATION's guard must be the READ's guard exactly (fix round,
	// D2): a texture declared where the piece does not read it is a dead
	// uniform, but a piece that reads one that was not declared is a compile
	// error that loses the frame. JahProbeGather_piece_ps.any carries the
	// same six terms and the reason for each.
	@property( jah_probe_gather && hlms_screen_pos_int && needs_env_brdf && !hlms_prepass && !hlms_shadowcaster && !irradiance_volumes )
		vulkan_layout( ogre_t@value(jahProbeIrradiance) ) uniform texture2D jahProbeIrradiance;
	@end
	// THE CLOUD FIELD (CLOUDS-2D-1): the layer's vertical optical depth, one
	// tile of it, wrapping. Declared wherever the pass claimed its slot; read
	// only by the shadow term below, whose guard is narrower (a prepass or a
	// material that receives no shadow declares it and never reads it).
	@property( jah_cloud_shadow )
		vulkan_layout( ogre_t@value(jahCloudField) ) uniform texture2D jahCloudField;
		@property( syntax == glslvk )
			layout( ogre_s@value(jahCloudField) ) uniform sampler jahCloudSampler;
		@end
	@end
	// THE SUN CONTACT VISIBILITY (PHOTON-RAYS-1): R8, 1 = the sun reaches the
	// surface this texel's ray started from. Declared wherever the pass claimed
	// its slot (the view's PrePassUse pass alone); read by
	// JahSunContact_piece_ps.any with a texel fetch, so no sampler is declared.
	@property( jah_sun_contact )
		vulkan_layout( ogre_t@value(jahSunVis) ) uniform texture2D jahSunVis;
	@end
	// THE PLANET'S ATMOSPHERE'S TABLES (SKY-ATMOSPHERE-1): the sky view and the
	// aerial-perspective volume, both read with the environment's trilinear
	// clamped block (one sampler per slot, the pair bound by
	// FogHlmsListener::hlmsTypeChanged), then the model's arithmetic (the piece
	// the build wraps from src/rayquery/include/jah_atmosphere.glsl) and the two
	// reads the fog below makes. The tables hold radiance for a sun of unit
	// illuminance; atmoSettings.skyE is the sun at the top of the air.
	@property( jah_atmo_ap )
		vulkan_layout( ogre_t@value(jahAtmoSky) ) uniform texture2D jahAtmoSky;
		vulkan_layout( ogre_t@value(jahAtmoAerial) ) uniform texture3D jahAtmoAerial;
		@property( syntax == glslvk )
			layout( ogre_s@value(jahAtmoSky) ) uniform sampler jahAtmoSkySampler;
			layout( ogre_s@value(jahAtmoAerial) ) uniform sampler jahAtmoAerialSampler;
		@end
		@insertpiece( JahAtmosphere )
		// The light the air scatters towards the eye (xyz, unit sun) and the
		// transmittance (w) between the eye and `km` along the world direction.
		float4 jahAtmoAerialAt( float3 dir, float km )
		{
			const float2 uv = jahAtmoDirUv( dir, atmoSettings.sunDir.xyz, atmoSettings.planet, float2( 32.0, 64.0 ) );
			const float w = jahAtmoApW( km, atmoSettings.planet, 32.0 );
			return OGRE_SampleLevel( jahAtmoAerial, jahAtmoAerialSampler, float3( uv, w ), 0.0 );
		}
		// The sky's radiance (unit sun) at the direction's azimuth, held above the
		// horizon: what a medium that hides the planet fades towards.
		float3 jahAtmoSkyAbove( float3 dir )
		{
			const float2 uv = jahAtmoDirUvAbove( dir, atmoSettings.sunDir.xyz, atmoSettings.planet, float2( 192.0, 108.0 ) );
			return OGRE_SampleLevel( jahAtmoSky, jahAtmoSkySampler, uv, 0.0 ).xyz;
		}
	@end
@end
@end

// THE ATMOSPHERE COMPONENT'S CONST BUFFER (SKY-ATMOSPHERE-1; OgreAtmosphere.cpp
// AtmoSettingsGpu is the writer): the piece the stock vertex and pixel shaders
// insert where the component's struct goes. The first three floats are the
// names upstream's fog block reads.
@property( jah_atmo_buf )
@piece( AtmosphereNprSkyStructDecl )
	struct JahAtmoSettings
	{
		float fogDensity;
		float fogBreakMinBrightness;
		float fogBreakFalloff;
		float aerialScale;
		float4 skyE;
		float4 sunDir;
		float4 planet;
	};
	CONST_BUFFER( JahAtmoSettingsBuf, @value(jah_atmo_buf) )
	{
		JahAtmoSettings atmoSettings;
	};
@end
@end

// THE CLOUD LAYER'S SHADOW ON THE GROUND (CLOUDS-2D-1; SPECS/CLOUDS_ASSESSMENT.md
// section 3.3). The sun's term is multiplied by the fraction of its beam that
// crosses the cloud sheet unscattered on the way to this pixel: the sun ray
// from the pixel meets the sheet (altitude jahCloudSun.z) at the pixel's world
// xz thrown towards the sun by (altitude - y) / tan(elevation), and there the
// beam crosses exp( -tau / mu_s ) of it -- the SAME field and the same
// Beer-Lambert slab the layer in the sky is drawn with.
//
// THE HOOK is the sun's own shadow factor: upstream multiplies the FIRST
// shadow-casting directional light's term by the piece named
// DarkenWithShadowFirstLight (Pbs/Any/ShadowMapping_piece_ps.any), and this
// library folder is parsed after that one, so the piece is replaced here by
// the same factor times the cloud's. That is Terra's pattern (its shadow map
// scales the same term) without claiming custom_ps_preLights, which the
// material graph's generated pieces own per datablock and a second
// definition of would fail to compile. The guard is the original piece's
// guard plus our pass property, so a pass with no cloud layer generates
// exactly the source it generated before this lane.
//
// A MATERIAL THAT RECEIVES NO SHADOWS is shaded all the same (the fix round's
// F2): upstream leaves the first-light piece undefined for it, so the same
// multiply is defined there on its own -- the sheet's transmittance is what it
// is, whatever the material says about shadow maps. And a SUN THAT CASTS NO
// SHADOW is drawn in upstream's non-caster directional loop, whose factor is
// the fork's custom_ps_darkenNonCasterDirectional hook: every directional light
// without a shadow map crosses the sheet along the SUN's throw (the one sun is
// what the map is thrown for; a second directional is an approximation). The
// // ambient is NOT scaled: the sheet is
// kilometres up, so the sky a ground point sees through it varies over a
// kernel as wide as the altitude -- uniform across any scene -- and that
// uniform part is already in the ambient, because the environment capture
// photographs the sheet.
@property( jah_cloud_shadow && hlms_lights_directional_non_caster && ( hlms_normal || hlms_qtangent ) && !hlms_shadowcaster && !hlms_prepass )
@piece( custom_ps_functions )
#define JAH_CLOUD_TAU( uv ) OGRE_SampleLevel( jahCloudField, jahCloudSampler, uv, 0.0 ).x
@insertpiece( JahCloudShadow )
midf jahCloudSunTransmittance( float3 viewPos )
{
	const float3 jahWp = float3( dot( passBuf.jahCloudInvView0.xyz, viewPos ) + passBuf.jahCloudInvView0.w,
								 dot( passBuf.jahCloudInvView1.xyz, viewPos ) + passBuf.jahCloudInvView1.w,
								 dot( passBuf.jahCloudInvView2.xyz, viewPos ) + passBuf.jahCloudInvView2.w );
	return midf_c( jahCloudTransmittance( jahWp, passBuf.jahCloudMap, passBuf.jahCloudSun ) );
}
@end
@piece( JahCloudSunFactor )* jahCloudSunTransmittance( inPs.pos.xyz )@end
@property( hlms_lights_directional )
	@property( receive_shadows && hlms_num_shadow_map_lights )
		@undefpiece( DarkenWithShadowFirstLight )
		@piece( DarkenWithShadowFirstLight )* ( fShadow @insertpiece( JahCloudSunFactor ) )@end
	@else
		@piece( DarkenWithShadowFirstLight )* jahCloudSunTransmittance( inPs.pos.xyz )@end
	@end
@end
@piece( custom_ps_darkenNonCasterDirectional )* jahCloudSunTransmittance( inPs.pos.xyz )@end
@end

@property( hlms_fog )

// Replace upstream's per-vertex sky colour. Redefinition needs the undef first
// (the parser rejects a duplicate piece) and needs this folder to be the LAST
// library folder.
//
// UNDER ANY SKY BUT THE ATMOSPHERE the fog colour is the authored one, out of
// the pass buffer, and upstream's own fog block does the distance fog with it.
//
// UNDER THE ATMOSPHERE (jah_atmo_ap, set by FogHlmsListener whenever it is the
// sky — the sky decides, there is no switch) THE WHOLE FOG IS PER PIXEL, below,
// and upstream's block is an exact identity (the component hands it a density
// of 0). The vertex colour is then not read, so it is written as zero.
//
// The height layer's interpolant is written in BOTH modes, so it cannot live in
// that piece: custom_vs_posExecution is inserted at the end of the same
// function (Hlms/Pbs/GLSL/VertexShader_vs.glsl:73), where worldPos is still in
// scope.
@undefpiece( DoAtmosphereNprSky )
@property( !jah_atmo_ap )
	@piece( DoAtmosphereNprSky )
		outVs.fog.xyz = midf3_c( passBuf.jahFogColour.xyz );
	@end
@else
	@piece( DoAtmosphereNprSky )
		outVs.fog.xyz = midf3_c( 0.0, 0.0, 0.0 );
	@end
@end

@property( hlms_normal || hlms_qtangent )
	@piece( custom_vs_posExecution )
		outVs.jahFogWorldY = worldPos.y;
	@end
@end

@property( hlms_normal || hlms_qtangent )
	@piece( custom_VStoPS )
		INTERPOLANT( float jahFogWorldY, @counter(texcoord) );
	@end

	// The fog writes outPs_colour0, which is #defined to `outColour`
	// (Hlms/Common/GLSL/CrossPlatformSettings_piece_all.glsl) — and outColour is
	// only DECLARED when the shader actually writes colour: not in a shadow
	// caster, not in a depth/normal prepass, not in a depth-only pass
	// (Hlms/Pbs/GLSL/PixelShader_ps.glsl). Referencing it there throws out of
	// renderOneFrame and the frame goes black with one line in the log. The
	// compositor-chain lane learned this on the old fog piece (irisgl 92e9833);
	// it is carried forward here rather than re-learned when the SSR prepass
	// lands. (The built-in fog block upstream is guarded the same way.) Both
	// branches run after upstream's block, on the colour about to be written;
	// the second is the height layer exactly as it was before FOG-ATMO-1.
	// ...AND NOT UNDER THE PHOTON VIEW'S ISOLATION (jah_photon_view, JahPhotonView_piece_ps.any),
	// which owns this hook for its pass and draws one lighting term with no fog at all.
	@property( !hlms_shadowcaster && !hlms_prepass && !hlms_render_depth_only && !jah_photon_view )
	@piece( custom_ps_posExecution )
	@property( jah_atmo_ap )
	{
		// THE WHOLE FOG, PER PIXEL, UNDER THE PLANET'S ATMOSPHERE (the header
		// of this section). Ogre-Next 4.0 hardcodes hw_gamma_write to 1
		// (OgreHlmsPbs preparePassHash), i.e. the shader emits LINEAR and the
		// target encodes; the other branches are the correct answer if that
		// ever changes.
		const float jahL = length( inPs.pos.xyz );
		@property( !hw_gamma_write )
			const float3 jahSurf = float3( outPs_colour0.xyz ) * float3( outPs_colour0.xyz );
		@else
			const float3 jahSurf = float3( outPs_colour0.xyz );
		@end
		// The pixel's own ray: the view-space position turned into world axes
		// by the pass's view rotation (the particle system's idiom), so a probe
		// face or a mirror camera asks its own direction.
		const float3 jahDir = normalize( mul( toFloat3x3( passBuf.view ), inPs.pos.xyz ) );

		// THE AIR (SKY-ATMOSPHERE-1): the aerial-perspective table at this ray
		// and this distance times the aerial scale — the light the air between
		// the eye and the surface scatters in (xyz, times the sun at the top of
		// the air) and what of the surface survives it (w). Scale 0 reads the
		// table's first slice, the eye itself: exactly (0, 0, 0, 1).
		const float4 jahAp = jahAtmoAerialAt( jahDir, jahL * 0.001 * atmoSettings.aerialScale );
		float3 jahOut = jahSurf * jahAp.w + jahAp.xyz * atmoSettings.skyE.xyz;

		// THE WORLD FOG, ON TOP: its own medium, fogging towards the sky just
		// above the horizon at this azimuth (a fog thick enough to hide the
		// ground reads as the horizon sky behind it — no line). The breakthrough
		// bends it on the unfogged colour's luminance, clamped to [0; 1]
		// (upstream's max( exp2, 0 ) is 1.017 at luminance 0 with the shipped
		// pair, which lerped PAST the fog colour).
		const float3 jahFogLin = jahAtmoSkyAbove( jahDir ) * atmoSettings.skyE.xyz;
		const float jahLum = dot( jahSurf, float3( 0.212655, 0.715158, 0.072187 ) );
		const float jahBreak = clamp( exp2( atmoSettings.fogBreakFalloff * jahLum +
											atmoSettings.fogBreakMinBrightness ), 0.0, 1.0 );
		const float jahTd = lerp( 1.0, exp2( -jahL * passBuf.jahFogHeight.w ), jahBreak );
		jahOut = lerp( jahFogLin, jahOut, jahTd );
		if( passBuf.jahFogColour.w > 0.0 )
		{
			// The height layer (its integral is written out in the other branch),
			// in the same sky colour.
			const float jahDy   = inPs.jahFogWorldY - passBuf.jahFogHeight.z;
			const float jahA    = exp2( clamp( -passBuf.jahFogHeight.x *
											   ( passBuf.jahFogHeight.z - passBuf.jahFogHeight.y ),
											   -60.0, 60.0 ) );
			const float jahU    = clamp( passBuf.jahFogHeight.x * jahDy * 0.6931472, -60.0, 60.0 );
			const float jahRamp = abs( jahU ) < 0.001 ? ( 1.0 - 0.5 * jahU )
													  : ( ( 1.0 - exp( -jahU ) ) / jahU );
			const float jahT    = exp2( -passBuf.jahFogColour.w * jahA * jahL * jahRamp );
			jahOut = lerp( jahFogLin, jahOut, jahT );
		}
		@property( !hw_gamma_write )
			outPs_colour0.xyz = midf3_c( sqrt( jahOut ) );
		@else
			outPs_colour0.xyz = midf3_c( jahOut );
		@end
	}
	@else
	if( passBuf.jahFogColour.w > 0.0 )
	{
		// Height layer: density( y ) = D * 2^( -k * ( y - y0 ) ), integrated along the
		// view ray. With u = k * dy * ln2 the integral is D * A * L * (1 - e^-u) / u,
		// where A = 2^( -k * ( camY - y0 ) ), L = eye distance and dy the world-Y rise
		// from the camera to this pixel. The (1 - e^-u)/u factor tends to 1 as u -> 0
		// (a level ray sees constant density); the clamps keep the exponentials finite
		// for extreme falloff values instead of producing NaNs.
		const float jahL    = length( inPs.pos.xyz );
		const float jahDy   = inPs.jahFogWorldY - passBuf.jahFogHeight.z;
		const float jahA    = exp2( clamp( -passBuf.jahFogHeight.x *
										   ( passBuf.jahFogHeight.z - passBuf.jahFogHeight.y ),
										   -60.0, 60.0 ) );
		const float jahU    = clamp( passBuf.jahFogHeight.x * jahDy * 0.6931472, -60.0, 60.0 );
		const float jahRamp = abs( jahU ) < 0.001 ? ( 1.0 - 0.5 * jahU )
												  : ( ( 1.0 - exp( -jahU ) ) / jahU );
		const float jahT    = exp2( -passBuf.jahFogColour.w * jahA * jahL * jahRamp );
		// The built-in fog mixes in linear space, before the shader's gamma write;
		// this runs after it, so the fog colour is matched to whatever space the
		// output is in. Ogre-Next 4.0 hardcodes hw_gamma_write to 1 (OgreHlmsPbs
		// preparePassHash), i.e. the shader always emits linear and the target
		// encodes -- the first branch is the correct answer if that ever changes.
		@property( !hw_gamma_write )
			const midf3 jahFogCol = midf3_c( sqrt( passBuf.jahFogColour.xyz ) );
		@else
			const midf3 jahFogCol = midf3_c( passBuf.jahFogColour.xyz );
		@end
		outPs_colour0.xyz = lerp( jahFogCol, outPs_colour0.xyz, midf_c( jahT ) );
	}
	@end
	@end
	@end
@end

@end

// Jahshaka's base-map UV transform — the document's PbrMaterial texture
// scale/offset/rotation. HlmsPbs has no UV transform for its base maps (detail
// maps alone get offset/scale), so this redefines Ogre's official UV-modifier
// macros (UvModifierMacros_piece_ps.any, inserted at the top of every Pbs pixel
// shader) to transform each base-map lookup by the per-datablock user values
// that OgreScene::applyPbr writes with setUserValue. userValue lives in the
// material buffer: tiling, offset and rotation edits are const-buffer updates,
// never shader rebuilds. Deliberately OUTSIDE the fog property above:
// alpha-tested (Cutout) caster shaders sample the diffuse map through
// UV_DIFFUSE with `material` in scope too, and must see the same transform as
// the colour pass or shadows detach from the silhouette. UV_SPECULAR covers the
// metalness map (metallic workflow rides the specular texture slot). No AO
// macro exists — HlmsPbs has no AO input (see Types.h).
//
// THE FORM IS AFFINE ON PURPOSE:
//     uv' = M * (uv * s) + b
//   userValue[0].xy = s          the per-axis tiling
//   userValue[0].zw = b          the bias, ALREADY including the rotation of
//                                the offset about the texture centre
//   userValue[1]    = M          row-major 2x2 rotation
// The authored expression is R * ((uv*s + o) - 0.5) + 0.5; distributing R and
// precomputing b = R*(o - 0.5) + 0.5 on the CPU is what keeps the untransformed
// case EXACT — at the identity M is I and b is (0,0), so this reduces to
// uv*s, bit-for-bit the expression that was here before rotation existed. A
// shader-side centre round-trip would have shifted every material in every
// scene by an ulp. See OgreMaterials.cpp applyPbr for the CPU half.
@piece( custom_ps_uv_modifier_macros )
	#undef UV_DIFFUSE
	#undef UV_NORMAL
	#undef UV_SPECULAR
	#undef UV_ROUGHNESS
	#undef UV_EMISSIVE
	#define JAH_UV_XFORM(x) (float2( dot( material.userValue[1].xy, (x) * material.userValue[0].xy ), dot( material.userValue[1].zw, (x) * material.userValue[0].xy ) ) + material.userValue[0].zw)
	#define UV_DIFFUSE(x) JAH_UV_XFORM(x)
	#define UV_NORMAL(x) JAH_UV_XFORM(x)
	#define UV_SPECULAR(x) JAH_UV_XFORM(x)
	#define UV_ROUGHNESS(x) JAH_UV_XFORM(x)
	// A LIGHTMAP rides the emissive slot (emissiveAsLightmap) and is authored in
	// UV space, never tiled: the material's tiling must not touch it (bake-
	// foundations audit F1, 2026-09-09). Off the property, the emissive map is a
	// map like the others and tiles with them.
	@property( !emissive_as_lightmap )
	#define UV_EMISSIVE(x) JAH_UV_XFORM(x)
	@end
	@property( emissive_as_lightmap )
	#define UV_EMISSIVE(x) (x)
	@end
@end
